{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1429237-flora-of-the-fallen-realms","id":1429237,"title":"Flora of the Fallen Realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-20T14:27:02-08:00","id":1429237,"title":"Flora of the Fallen Realms","content":"Maybe a question asked before, and I'm truly sorry if I'm reposting, but is there a mention of some of the weird flora of Fallen Realms?<br /> Plants unique to Underworld or Shadow Realm?<br /> Also, is there something connected to herbalism or brewing among the Awakened? Besides the usual Imbuing of liquids with a spell effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T15:22:58-08:00","id":1429248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1429237-flora-of-the-fallen-realms#post1429237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is there something connected to herbalism or brewing among the Awakened? Besides the usual Imbuing of liquids with a spell effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>A plant or herb from another realm would could as a +3 Sacrament Yantra if sacrificed for a spell. This could obviously also be used as part of a brew.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T15:45:21-08:00","id":1429252,"title":"","content":"&quot;The living can find things to eat in the<br /> Underworld, be it weird fungi in the tunnels<br /> of the Upper Reaches or a luxuriant meal of<br /> Barghest Essence cooked up in one of the River<br /> Cities. While it may seem filling and possibly<br /> even flavorful, none of it will sustain a living<br /> body. To dine on the fare of the Underworld is<br /> to dine on ash without realizing it, the first hint<br /> of the hunger is not an ache in the belly but<br /> a lightness in the head. Some starve to death<br /> without ever realizing why, only to wake up<br /> experiencing an entirely new kind of hunger.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sidebar on page 203 in Geist: The Sin-Eaters Second Edition.<br /> <br /> So, no unique plants in the Underworld, no. What exists, is either just the ghosts of plants from the material or the Underworld itself taking the shape of plants. Neither is nourishing (for the living) nor do they have any effects that couldn't be gained from other Castoffs or from stones just laying around in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T18:05:01-08:00","id":1429275,"title":"","content":"Changeling has a lot of material on the goblin fruits and oddments that grow in the Hedge, and Demon has some cryptoflora (plants supernaturally mutated by exposure to aether) sprinkled across the corebook, Storyteller's Guide, and Night Horrors: Enemy Action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}